course: dictionary
lesson: 7197
title: A borrowed word: petite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some English words came from other languages. Petite was borrowed from French. It means small and slim, and people often use it in a polite, kind way about a girl or a woman.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Shops use «petite sizes» for clothes made for shorter women, so the word can describe clothes as well as people. When a word is borrowed, its meaning usually stays close to the original, even if the spelling or sound changes a little.
explain: French has a sound trick. Petit is for a boy or a male thing, and petite is for a girl or a female thing. The final e makes the t sound: «puh-TEE» becomes «puh-TEET». In French, the describing word matches the person it describes, as in «Ma sœur est petite».
fact: Petite is an adjective, a describing word.
fact: «Petite» means small, short and slim in a pretty way, used of a girl or woman.
fact: In shops, «petite» sizes are clothes for shorter women.
fact: In French, the e at the end of «petite» makes the t sound: «puh-TEET».
fact: Words borrowed from another language often keep their original meaning.
exercise: «She was petite, so the coat in her size was easy to find.» What does petite mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Very old | *Small and slim | Very tall and strong
exercise: A shop sign says «Petite sizes now in store.» Where would you find these? | Toys for babies | Tools for a garden | Food for a party | *Clothes for shorter women
exercise: In French, «petit» is used for a boy, and «petite» for a girl. What does the final e tell you? | *The word describes a girl or woman | The word is a plural | The word is a question | The word describes a very old thing
test: Petite is a word borrowed from which language? | Spanish | *French | Gen Alpha slang | Scots
test: The French word for a small boy is «petit». What makes «petite» different? | It has no sound change at all | *It is for a girl or woman, and ends with an e | It means very old | It is for a boy, and ends with a t
exam: «The petite gymnast flipped across the mat.» What does petite most likely mean? | Dangerous and wet | Very heavy and slow | Old and grey | *Small, slim and neat
